{"etape": 11, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-21T12:45:39.958199Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "Great — based on your plans, here's my analysis:\n\n**1. Arriving in New York from Dallas on May 17th:**\n- ✅ **Keep `5BGGWZ`** — its return leg is **DFW → EWR (Newark)** on May 17, which is exactly \"Dallas → New York area\" arriving that day.\n- ❌ **Cancel `FDZ0T5`** — this is JFK → ORD → PHL on May 17. It departs from New York rather than arriving there, and doesn't match your Dallas → New York plan.\n\n**2. Leaving Boston on May 22nd:**\n- ✅ **Keep `PUNERT`** — this is **BOS → MIA → DEN** departing Boston on May 22. Matches \"leaving Boston.\"\n- ❌ **Cancel `HSR97W`** — this is ORD → PHL → SFO on May 22, departing Chicago. Doesn't match.\n\nSo I'd propose cancelling **`FDZ0T5`** and **`HSR97W`**, and keeping **`5BGGWZ`** and **`PUNERT`**.\n\nBefore I proceed, two things:\n1. Could you tell me the **reason for cancellation**? (Options: change of plan, airline cancelled the flight, or other reasons.)\n2. Just to confirm — both `FDZ0T5` and `HSR97W` are **business** class, so they're eligible for cancellation, and refunds would go back to your original payment method within 5–7 business days.\n\nShall I go ahead and cancel those two reservations once you confirm the reason?"}, "resultat": "Yes, that sounds correct. Please go ahead and cancel `FDZ0T5` and `HSR97W`. The reason for cancellation is a change of plan.\n\nI might have reservations for other passengers on my profile, but I don't want to modify those. Just my own flights.", "erreur": null}
